# Pentatonic Box 3 Lick (repertoire plan: st-pent-box-3). An original 8-bar study in A minor
# pentatonic box 3, frets 9 to 13, over a one-chord Am7 groove. Four 2-bar phrases in call and
# response: phrases 1 and 3 ask (they stop on E and on C, chord tones that leave the door open),
# phrases 2 and 4 answer (they come home to A: the A on string 5, then the A on string 2).
# All 12 notes of the box are used, and nothing else.
# Fingering as the Scales screen shows the box: the hand sits at the 10th fret, finger 1 on fret 10
# and finger 3 on fret 12 (strings 6, 5, 4 and 1); on string 3 finger 1 reaches back to fret 9 and
# finger 4 takes fret 12; on string 2 finger 1 is back on fret 10 and finger 4 takes fret 13.
# The pull-off ends the study: finger 4 on string 2 fret 13 (C) pulls off to finger 1 on fret 10 (A).
